  - Checks: typecheck, Biome, the public check, the touched test files, `npm run docs:build` and `npm run docs:check` before each commit. The full `npm run check` ran once: 1,056 of 1,058 tests passed. One failure was this goal's own goal-mode held-out test, whose two runs per case gave too wide an interval on a loaded machine; it now takes three runs and a lower threshold, and passes alone and beside the judge's tests. The other, Metrics' "today" in `src/control/usage-ui.test.ts`, fails in the first hour after midnight in the time zone it names, whatever the code: its bars need two hours of today.
  - Pages: the kit manifest reference, Write a kit, Verdicts and states, Contract, Exports, MCP tools, the REST API, the command line, Knowledge base, Campaign modes, Your first goal campaign, Why agents never judge, Agents, lanes and the planner, Supervision, Isolation, How it fits together, the roadmap; the changelog.
  - The judge, agents, control and multi-GPU compose acceptances run at roll time.
- 2026-10-22: Fixes from a review of this goal and goal 081.
  - A kit's time limits (a cell's `timeout_s`, and `build`, `run` and `check`'s) are at most 86400 s, the longest run the broker takes. A longer one passed the kit check, the broker refused its run under the id -1, the controller dropped that answer, and the judge's call never ended. The kit check now refuses it in words, and the broker answers a refused request under the request's own id. Tests: `src/harness/kit.test.ts`, `src/harness/broker/server.test.ts`.
  - An error in the judge's own work while held-out cells run (a kit's cell without a rate's `work` parameter threw `kit metric …: bad work … or time …`, with the run's time) became a `crash_infra` verdict whose reasons reach the lanes' briefs and the teachers' evidence. A held-out pass's error now reaches the verdict and Live only as `a held-out check could not finish (an infrastructure failure)`; the rig's log keeps it, for the owner. The champion's own held-out failure keeps its fixed words. The kit's check against the contract refuses a cell the contract runs without each rate's `work` parameter above zero, and New campaign scores a rate only when every case, hidden ones too, says its work done (it looked at the measured cases only, so a hidden case without it failed every held-out run). Tests: `src/harness/judge/held-out.test.ts`, `src/harness/kit.test.ts`, `src/control/campaign-builder.test.ts`.
  - Control's agent token read the owner's view over MCP: `get_run` gave each attempt's held-out cells with their values and thresholds, its timeline's `held_out_checked` bodies, and `goal_checks` with each held-out cell's time limit; `recent_events` gave the same events. For the agent token only, a held-out check is now `{at, pass, kinds, words}`, a `held_out_checked` body `{run, pass, kinds, words}`, and `goal_checks` lists no held-out cell (`src/control/agent-view.ts`). The owner, the operator and the reader keep the full view, as this goal's decision says ("for the owner"). Test: `src/harness/judge/held-out.test.ts`. Pages: MCP tools, Tokens, Verdicts and states.
  - A hill climb's `cells` and `held_out_cells` could share a cell, which was then measured at screening. The contract's check refuses it in words (`<cells> is in both cells and held_out_cells: …`, path `held_out_cells`); a valid contract's hash is unchanged. Test: `src/core/core.test.ts`. Page: Contract.
  - A comment in `src/harness/outbox.ts` still said held-out results never go into an export. The `held_out` table does not; the `held_out_checked` event, the owner's record, is in the events table and `events.jsonl` by this goal's decision, as the Exports page says. The comment says so now, and `src/harness/judge/judge.test.ts` checks the event is in the export's `events.jsonl`.

